\subsection{Pushdown}{

When a lazy plan over a scan runs through the optimizer (\code{compute()},
\code{collect()}), the scan reads only the columns the plan uses, and the
conditions of a \code{filter()} directly on the scan that libcudf can decide
exactly are given to the reader, which skips row groups from the file's
statistics and drops the other rows while decoding. \code{explain()} shows the
columns and the filter of the scan. A condition is pushed only when it is a
comparison of a column with a literal that converts to the column's file
type without change (\code{==}, \code{!=}, \code{<}, \code{<=}, \code{>}, \code{>=}) on an integer,
