\code{print()} and \code{glimpse()} of a table that is a bare scan (or only \code{select()}s
and \code{rename()}s of one) read just the first rows of the file, which libcudf
decodes as whole row groups: when the row group that holds them has more than
65,536 rows or 128 MB of column data, nothing is read and the schema is printed
instead (write files with smaller row groups, \verb{row_group_size =}, to get a
preview). Any other plan over a file prints its schema and is not run.
