the variable exists, so any value, \code{0} included, turns the switch on. To turn
it off, call \code{Sys.unsetenv("LIBCUDF_USE_DEBUG_STREAM_POOL")} after loading
cuplyr and before the first \code{read_parquet_gpu()} or \code{write_parquet_gpu()}
call in the session. A lazy \code{read_parquet_gpu()} counts too: it runs
libcudf's reader when it is called. libcudf creates its stream pool once, so
unsetting the variable later has no effect.
